OnRoute: Team Execution Brief

Team Teen Bahadur | Devmarketplace x NED AI Hackathon | Final day: 22 Oct 2026

Read this fully (3 minutes). It replaces the old context file. Goal: a working demo that is honest, polished and easy to understand.

1. What we are building

OnRoute helps NED students recover when their usual university shuttle ("point") plan fails.

It combines verified route data, recent student reports, and available travel estimates to compare realistic next steps: wait, board at a later stop, try another point, or use public transport / Bykea / inDrive.

Our edge: most "bus apps" fake live ETAs. OnRoute is honest about what it knows and what it doesn't. Judges will notice.

2. The 3 scenarios (everything we build serves these)
Point not coming today. Suggest other routes or transport options.
Point already left my stop. Can I catch it at a later stop? (This is our hero demo.)
Point is delayed. Should I wait or switch?
3. The one rule we never break

Every piece of info on screen must carry a label:

Label	Meaning
Scheduled	From the verified shuttle document
Reported	A student report, with timestamp
Estimated	Calculated, with assumptions shown
Unknown	Not enough data. Say so.
Stale	Report too old to trust
Conflicting	Recent reports disagree

Never show:

A live countdown to a real bus arrival (we have no live tracking).
"Cancelled" just because one student didn't see the bus.
Invented stops, times, fares or road closures.
Fake/demo data without a "DEMO DATA" label.

No reports = Unknown, not "all fine." The app must still be useful with zero reports.

4. Scope: what we build

Layer 1: Must work (the core)

Phone-friendly web app
Route/stop data from the shuttle PDF (1-2 routes, hand-verified)
Deterministic logic (plain code, NOT the AI) that compares options
The three scenarios, with the labels above

Layer 2: Build if the AI builder makes it easy

Login/signup (2FA only if the platform gives it cheaply)
One-tap reports: bus seen / departed / not seen / disruption (auto timestamp, freshness shown)
AI assistant that explains the computed options in plain language (must have a non-AI fallback)
Bykea/inDrive: student types the quote, app compares it
Map view

Layer 3: Pitch as roadmap, do NOT build

Live bus tracking, learned ETAs, road-closure feeds, rewards, native app, other universities
5. Owners (combine if we are fewer people)
Role	Job
Data owner	Extract 1-2 routes from the PDF into a table (stop names, order, times). Verify by hand. This is the bottleneck. Start now.
Logic owner	Decision logic + test against 3 hand-worked examples
Builder(s)	Prompt the AI builder for screens: journey form, results, report button, login
Demo/docs owner	README, final spec, demo script, backup video

Rule: one owner per area. Don't all edit the same thing.

